annot pair (1,3) with (3,1). L3: (1,3),(4,1) slope = (1-3)/(4-1) = -2/3, allowed. So L3: (1,3),(4,1). It also passes through (2,? ) maybe (2,? ) = y = -2/3*(2-1)+3 = -2/3+3 = 7/3 ≈ 2.333, not integer. So L3 covers (1,3),(4,1). Good.\n\nL4: (1,4),(2,1) slope = (1-4)/(2-1) = -3, allowed. So L4: (1,4),(2,1). It also passes through (3,-2) not needed.\n\nNow we have covered column 1 points: (1,1) L1, (1,2) L2, (1,3) L3, (1,4) L4. Column 2 points: (2,1) L4, (2,2) L1, (2,3) L2. Column 3 points: (3,1) not covered yet, (3,2) not covered yet. Column 4 point: (4,1) L3. So we still need to cover (3,1) and (3,2). We have used all 4 lines. So we need to adjust assignments to include (3,1) and (3,2) in some lines.\n\nWe could try to modify L4 to include (3,2) instead of (2,1). Let's see: L4 currently (1,4),(2,1). Could we replace (2,1) with (3,2)? Check slope between (1,4) and (3,2): (2-4)/(3-1) = -2/2 = -1, not allowed. So cannot.\n\nModify L3 to include (3,2) instead of (4,1). L3 currently (1,3),(4,1). Could we replace (4,1) with (3,2)? Slope between (1,3) and (3,2) = (2-3)/(3-1) = -1/2, allowed. So L3: (1,3),(3,2). Then (4,1) remains uncovered. Could we assign (4,1) to L2? L2 currently (1,2),(2,3). Slope = 1. Check if (4,1) lies on line y = x + 1? Actually line through (1,2) and (2,3) is y = x + 1. At x=4, y = 5, not 1. So no. Could assign (4,1) to L1? L1 is y = x, at x=4, y=4, not 1. Could assign (4,1) to L4? L4 is (1,4),(2,1) slope -3, equation y - 4 = -3(x - 1) => y = -3x + 7. At x=4, y = -12 + 7 = -5, not 1. So cannot.\n\nThus, we need to adjust more.\n\nMaybe we can use a different non-sunny line, like horizontal line y=1, covering many points in row 1: (1,1),(2,1),(3,1),(4,1),(5,1). That would cover column 5 point (5,1) and column 4 point (4,1) and column 3 point (3,1) and column 2 point (2,1) and column 1 point (1,1). Then we have 4 sunny lines left to cover the rest. Let's try that.\n\nUse non-sunny line y=1 (horizontal). That's not sunny (parallel to x-axis). It covers